	urldate = {2024-01-30},
	abstract = {Man-Machine Music shows just how diverse performances can be that arise from the interaction between humans and machines: composed by an AI, the piece was brought to life by human musicians and artists with the aid of classical as well as self-playing instruments and real-time visuals. The concept by Ars Electronica Futurelab artist and researcher Ali Nikrang in collaboration with visual artist Cori O'Lan was originally developed for the Ingolstadt Science Congress WIKOIN 2022 and performed there with the Georgian Chamber Orchestra.  At the Night Performances on Futurelab Day of the 2022 Ars Electronica Festival, Man-Machine Music was re-arranged and performed with the f.x.frenzel Quartet - Johanna Bohnen, Lui Chan, Bertin Christelbauer and Laura Maria Jungwirth -; accompanied by the lively, organic forms of Cori O'Lan's live visualizations. To find out more about Man-Machine Music, have a look at our blog https://ars.electronica.art/aeblog/en... To learn more about the Futurelab Day 2022, check out https://ars.electronica.art/futurelab... ------------------------------------------------------ Ars Electronica Futurelab: https://ars.electronica.art/futurelab... Ars Electronica https://ars.electronica.art/ ~~/~2881457~~ ~~/~arselectronica~~ ~~/~arselectronica~~ ~~/~arselectronica~~ https://www.flickr.com/photos/arselec...},
