	title = {Rhizomatic {{Learning}} in the {{Postmodern Era}}},
	url = {https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-19-9056-4_8},
	urldate = {2024-01-29},
	abstract = {The influence of a historical period, an epoch, on society, culture, and educationEducation is now recognized as indisputable in all types of academic discourse. Nowadays, all societal transformational processes are considered in the context of postmodernist philosophy. This chapter provides a methodologicalMethodology interpretation of the rhizomatic learningRhizomatic learning concept. It is noted that the rhizomaticRhizomatic structure itself is provisional and limitless; it destroys the traditional ideas about education as a centered and consistently defined structure. The study outlines the basic characteristics of the educational process such as: decentralizationDecentralization, multiplicityMultiplicity, discreteness, connectivity and heterogeneity, cartography, subjectivitySubjectivity, anti-binarismAnti-binarism, and some others. The purpose of this chapter is to describe the complex dynamic process the aim of which is to show students ways of independently acquiring and extracting knowledge and to help them form an interdisciplinary vision of the world, but not to fill their consciousness with specific knowledge and skills. The results of the study are illustrated with examples of Russian educational institutions, and they prove that the postmodern era imposes its own requirements on educationEducation, which consist not only of ensuring high quality of education, but also rejecting universal theories and the knowledge paradigm, and in transition to multiplicityMultiplicity and constant updating.},
	bdsk-url-1 = {https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-19-9056-4_8}}

