	url = {http://journal.telospress.com/content/1983/57/93},
	urldate = {2024-01-29},
	volume = {1983},
	abstract = {Rock music permeates all areas of social life, from supermarkets to homes. The intensity of its reception ranges from the fanatical devotion of youth subcultures to cheery accompaniment for household chores. The following deals primarily with analysis of the stars in rock music and its relation to consumerism. It does not pretend to be exhaustive of its subject --- other obviously important factors like sexuality are artificially left aside. Marxism has tended to attack rock music (and earlier, swing music) because of its commodity basis, and upheld folk music as ideologically superior. The American Communist Party consciously used folk music as part of its political strategy in the 1930s and 40s.},
