	abstract = {Sociological categories of youth widely used in political rhetoric and educational policy making are limited by the neoliberal discourses and humanist tradition within which they are constructed. Utilising a Deleuzian approach in order to trouble the very concept of youth itself affords opportunities to rethink youth as rhizome; unlinked from the traditional categories of age, class, race and gender. Instead, youth becomes an assemblage of multiplicities combining in radical and different ways to form a becoming-youth that is particular to this time.},
