	volume = {85},
	abstract = {Roger Scruton's account of the nature of music and our experience of it foregrounds the imagination. It is a particularly interesting and promising `non-realist' view in the aesthetics of music, in the sense that it does not postulate aesthetic properties of music that we represent in musical experience. In this paper I critically examine both Scruton's view and his main argument for it.},
